======================================================================================================================
  LVD residual   rho = +0.5476, EXACT p = 0.1710 (1.37 sigma)
  LVD -log M* alone rho = +0.3952, EXACT p = 0.3331 (0.97 sigma)
  LVD rank partial(residual, beta | logM*) = +0.4273; Pearson partial = +0.5816
  branch assignments that FLIP between the two compilations: ['Leo II']
  [FAIL] V9 (THE CORROBORATION IS WEAKER THAN QUOTED, AND IT DISAGREES ABOUT THE CAUSE) the second compilation must support the claim at a comparable strength AND attribute the signal to the same thing   (the LVD leg is quoted as rho = +0.548 without its p-value, which is 0.171 = 1.37 sigma -- NOT the '1.74 sigma both footings' the claim advertises. And the two compilations disagree about what carries the signal: on the f09 table mass alone BEATS the framework (+0.683 vs +0.667), on LVD it does not (+0.395 vs +0.548). Also, the quoted 'two residual vectors agree at r = +0.955' is near-guaranteed and is not evidence: R_half cancels identically on the isolated branch, so the compilations can differ only through M* and sigma -- and one object (['Leo II']) silently changes branch between them)

